AliasMode: window positions a page reads or sets are on the screen the
identity claims.

screen.availLeft/availTop can place the identity's screen elsewhere than the
real one, for example on a second monitor at x=1920. window.screenX used to
return the config's window.screenX whatever the window did, while
mozInnerScreenX and MouseEvent.screenX reported the real screen, so a page saw
the window's frame thousands of pixels away from its own content area.

screenX/screenY now report the real window position shifted by the offset
between the claimed and the real available area of the window's screen.
mozInnerScreenX/Y and trusted pointer events get the same shift, and
moveTo/moveBy take a position on the claimed screen. Chrome code and events a
page builds itself keep their own coordinates.

diff --git a/dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp b/dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp
index 7f6ea88..bbdc867 100644
--- a/dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp
+++ b/dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp
@@ -3636,7 +3636,27 @@ CSSIntPoint nsGlobalWindowOuter::GetScreenXY(CallerType aCallerType,
   aError = treeOwnerAsWin->GetPosition(&windowPos.x.value, &windowPos.y.value);
 
   CSSToLayoutDeviceScale scale = CSSToDevScaleForBaseWindow(treeOwnerAsWin);
-  return RoundedToInt(windowPos / scale);
+  CSSIntPoint position = RoundedToInt(windowPos / scale);
+  if (aCallerType != CallerType::System) {
+    position += ClaimedScreenOffset();
+  }
+  return position;
+}
+
+// Camoufox: screen.availLeft/availTop can claim a screen other than the real
+// one, such as a second monitor. Every position a page reads (screenX,
+// mozInnerScreenX, a pointer event's screenX) or sets (moveTo) is shifted by
+// this offset, so they agree with each other and with the claimed screen the
+// way they do on a real desktop. Chrome code keeps real positions.
+CSSIntPoint nsGlobalWindowOuter::ClaimedScreenOffset() {
+  RefPtr<nsScreen> screen = GetScreen();
+  nsDeviceContext* context = nsLayoutUtils::GetDeviceContextForScreenInfo(this);
+  if (!screen || !context) {
+    return {};
+  }
+  CSSIntPoint real =
+      CSSIntRect::FromAppUnitsRounded(context->GetClientRect()).TopLeft();
+  return CSSIntPoint(screen->AvailLeft(), screen->AvailTop()) - real;
 }
 
